{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519997-w5-hotpatch-reaching-the-spirit","id":1519997,"title":"[W5 Hotpatch] Reaching the Spirit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-06T17:56:54-07:00","id":1519997,"title":"[W5 Hotpatch] Reaching the Spirit","content":"This mechanical bit is in place of Harano and Hauglosk. If you are using it, do not use those as well*. I'm shooting from the hip here, as someone who treated the prospect of giving PDX money for the book the Excalibur Face, so a lot of this might not exactly fit.<br /> <br /> Reaching the Spirit: As a counterbalance to Rage, Garou are also conduits of the essential forces of the cosmos, heirs to both the physical matter of the world and also the ephemera of the Umbra. As natives of that place, they can return to it with some degree of ease, as well as channel the powers of spirits. Engaging in this activity is called a Reaching Roll; successes add to a Trait similar to but in some ways counter to Rage, Essence, which gives the werewolf greater capability for interacting and dealing with spirits, as well as traversing the Umbra. Generally, Reaching Rolls and Rage Rolls are not made in the same turn; the Garou must choose between which force they are being pulled.<br /> <br /> Essence Levels and Effects<br /> 0: You are distant from the spirit world. Getting back in touch with it will take some difficulty, possibly a jump start from a powerful spirit or another Garou. If you end up in the Umbra but still remain at this level of Essence, you suffer from the experience as per the typical rules of W5, but probably not for long, as being on the other side is a great way to at least try to get back in touch with it.<br /> 1: You have awakened your half-ephemeral nature. You can attempt to step sideways outside of caerns, but it takes five minutes to make the crossing. You only need to spend one Willpower per day to remain there, at most. Most Garou are at least this in touch with their spiritual nature.<br /> 2: It's becoming more apparent now that you're just as much a native of the Umbra as the world of matter and flesh. You can step sideways outside of caerns, and it only takes one minute to do so. You only need to spend one Willpower per week in the Umbra to remain there, at most. Social interaction actions with spirits gain one die.<br /> 3: Your reserves of primal power are great indeed. You can step sideways outside a caern, and it only take 15 seconds. You no longer need to spend Willpower to remain in the Umbra. Social interactions with spirits gain three dice.<br /> 4: At this point, your spiritual nature begins overtaking your physical one. You can return to the Umbra instantaneously from any point in the physical world, but it take a minute to return to the physical world. If you do not spend a point of Willpower once per month, you find yourself returning to the Umbra for an entire day if not already there, and you must remain there for a day before crossing back over. Social interactions with spirits gain three dice, and you can trade dice for automatic successes in these interactions at the rate of 1 per three dice.<br /> 5: Per the old cliche, some doubt that you are only half-spirit. You can return to the Umbra instantaneously from any point in the physical world, but it takes three minutes to return to the physical world. If you do not spend a point of Willpower once per week, you find yourself pulled back into the Umbra and must stay there for three days before crossing back into the physical world. Social interactions with spirits gain four dice, and you gain automatic successes at the rate of one per two dice. If you end up succeeding at a disconnection roll while in the Umbra at this level of Essence, you technically die and become an ancestor spirit, but this process will be painless and pleasant.<br /> <br /> Reaching Checks<br /> <br /> Disconnection: Spending an excessive amount of time in the physical world or Umbra can remove the influence of one side, to a detrimental degree. This roll differs based on where it happens, but not on the length of time, which is annually. If the Garou has not visited the Umbra in that time and remained in the physical world, roll their Essence. If the opposite occurs, roll Essence opposed by Rage. Any successes on the Essence roll while in the physical world maintain the character's Essence at its present level. Any net successes on the Essence roll in the Umbra increase the character's Essence by the number of successes, to a maximum of 5. Note that it takes at least a year maintaining Essence 5 to be in danger of instant transformation into an ancestor-spirit.<br /> <br /> Meditation: You may roll a Reaching check after meditating in a caern for several hours. Success increases the character's Essence by 1.<br /> <br /> Various Gifts and Rites: Many Gifts can be activated with a Reaching check instead of a Rage Check. Consult your &quot;legacy edition&quot; books and adjust as appropriate, but in general, it's most of them. At Essence 4 or 5, you don't even need to roll; activation is automatic.<br /> <br /> ___<br /> <br /> So, with this, the idea behind the balaance and danger is in being yanked out of the fight thanks to being too connected with the greater cosmos. But hey, it can take a while to get there, so you'll at least have some time to get shit done while you're on the razor's edge of Essence 5. It probably won't work that well without banging on it a lot more, but hopefully it's a start to conceptually putting Gnosis back in and getting rid of the hot mess of double-barreled degeneration mechanics (because just having on thing go down wasn't enough, PDX had to make them twice as screwed as vampires).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}